hyan Exploration Inc./Exploration Schyan Inc. and changed its name to Trulieve Cannabis Corp. in September 2018. Trulieve Cannabis Corp. was incorporated in 1940 and is headquartered in Tallahassee, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Kimberly  Rivers J.D. | Founder, Chairman & CEO | Age 47 | Compensation: $5.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $236K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $46K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 22\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Trulieve Cannabis Corp. Subordi is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.9B market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding. Operating margins are contracting by -2.2pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 60% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $229M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 19 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 2.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet 